  "text": "### Review Summary (`needs_changes`)\n\n#### Findings\n- **[blocker]** `packages/excalidraw/tests/selection.test.tsx:1498` \u2014 In `describe(\"lasso selection modes\")`, `drawLasso` calls `h.app.setActiveTool({ type: \"lasso\" })` unconditionally before every gesture, which resets `selectedElementIds` prior to the Shift+lasso gesture at line 1878 and causes `assertSelectedElements([frame.id, standaloneRect.id])` at line 1887 to fail.\n  - **Fix:** Activate the lasso tool in `renderWithBoxSelectionMode` (or guard `h.app.setActiveTool({ type: \"lasso\" })` in `drawLasso` with `if (h.state.activeTool.type !== \"lasso\")`) so Shift-modified lasso gestures retain the previous selection.\n\n#### Passing Checks\n- **Correctness (`lasso/utils.ts`, `lasso/index.ts`, `CHANGELOG.md`):** Implements `boxSelectionMode` (`\"contain\"` and `\"overlap\"`) enclosure, bound-text handling, and scene-wide top-level group containment per `change_plan.md`.\n- **Type safety & Lint:** `yarn test:typecheck` and `yarn test:code` pass with 0 errors/warnings.\n- **DRY:** Shared `getLassoSegments` helper extracted in `packages/excalidraw/lasso/utils.ts`.\n- **Unit tests (`tests/lasso.test.tsx`):** All unit tests for `\"contain\"` and `\"overlap\"` modes pass; snapshots unchanged.",
